# Understood by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages alike.

# Legacy paths that 301 on the live WordPress site. The rebuild serves the
# canonical page but not the old path, so inbound links, bookmarks and anything
# still sitting in search results would break at go-live. Found by comparing
# the two sites page by page rather than by crawling our own build, which is
# why the internal link check never flagged them: nothing on the rebuild points
# at these, but plenty out on the web still does.
/charity-information            /about-us/charity-information/                    301
/awareness-and-education        /aims-and-objectives/awareness-and-education/     301
/research-and-access-to-drugs   /aims-and-objectives/research-and-access-to-drugs/ 301
/patient-treatment-and-care     /aims-and-objectives/patient-treatment-and-care/  301
/2022/06/elementor-3229         /2022/06/honouring-emma-hillier/                  301

# The editor. TinaCloud links to /admin without a trailing slash, and the
# catch-all below would otherwise hand that to the 404 page — which is exactly
# what a client would see after clicking "Edit with TinaCMS". Serving it
# directly, rather than redirecting, keeps the address the editor was opened
# at so its hash routing is not disturbed.
/admin      /admin/index.html   200
/admin/*    /admin/index.html   200

# --- WordPress taxonomy URLs -------------------------------------------
# 420 addresses in the live sitemap that this site has no equivalent for.
# Generated by build/make-legacy-redirects.js from the live sitemaps.

# Categories are our topics under an older name. uncategorized is the one
# with nothing to point at, so it goes first — these are read in order.
/category/uncategorized/*                     /latest-news/                             301
/category/:slug/*                             /news/topic/:slug/                        301
/category/*                                   /latest-news/                             301

# 10 of the 380 tags share a slug with a topic and can land on it.
/tag/alternative-therapies/*                  /news/topic/alternative-therapies/        301
/tag/data/*                                   /news/topic/data/                         301
/tag/diagnosis/*                              /news/topic/diagnosis/                    301
/tag/drug-approval/*                          /news/topic/drug-approval/                301
/tag/fundraising/*                            /news/topic/fundraising/                  301
/tag/help-us/*                                /news/topic/help-us/                      301
/tag/patient-advocacy/*                       /news/topic/patient-advocacy/             301
/tag/policy/*                                 /news/topic/policy/                       301
/tag/quality-of-life/*                        /news/topic/quality-of-life/              301
/tag/research/*                               /news/topic/research/                     301
# The rest were only ever a filing system; their posts are all still here.
/tag/*                                        /latest-news/                             301

